{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/spectralLayout(weight:maxIterations:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols\/graph\/spectrallayout(weight:maxiterations:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"spectralLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"text":" = { _ in 1 }, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","text":"NoConvergence","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","text":"Drawing","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A is the weighted adjacency matrix: parallel edges add their weights, self-loops are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ignored, and a weight of 0 is no edge. The eigenvalues are sorted ascending with their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"multiplicity, so a graph with c components has c zero eigenvalues and its axes come from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"eigenvectors of 0 when c > 1 (which ones is fixed by the solver, not specified). Each axis’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sign makes its first entry, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, whose magnitude is at least 10⁻⁴ of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"largest positive. Two vertices have y = 0, and one vertex is at the origin. The drawing is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not rescaled ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rescaled(scale:center:)"},{"type":"text","text":" maps it to a common frame). A directed graph is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drawn through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"undirectedView"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Dense: Householder tridiagonalization and the implicit QL iteration, O(n³) time and n²","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s, for graphs of up to a few thousand vertices.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","t